  "short_description": "List events, find free time, and inspect attendees across your Google Calendars.",
  "store_description": "Google's official hosted Calendar MCP server (Workspace Developer Preview). IMPORTANT: This server requires manual setup before it can be used. (1) Join the Google Workspace Developer Preview Program at https://developers.google.com/workspace/preview. (2) In your Google Cloud project, enable BOTH APIs: 'calendar-json.googleapis.com' (the REST API) and 'calendarmcp.googleapis.com' (the MCP service). (3) Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials with redirect URI 'http://127.0.0.1:3088/api/mcp/oauth/callback'. (4) In Google Auth Platform > Clients, open the OAuth client and check 'Use this client for an AI-powered agent'. This flag is MANDATORY from November 11, 2026 — Google will reject any OAuth client without it. (5) Set PELDRUN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and PELDRUN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET environment variables. (6) Add your Google account as a test user on the OAuth consent screen. Once configured, the server exposes read-only Calendar tools by default: calendar_list_events, calendar_get_event, calendar_list_calendars, calendar_find_free_time. Adding 'calendar.events' to the scopes list enables event creation and modification.",
  "description": "Official Google Calendar MCP server — list events and find free time.",
  "category": "productivity",
  "tags": ["google", "calendar", "events", "scheduling", "workspace", "meetings"],
